  "solution": {
    "text": "An oxide is a a binary compound of oxygen with another element or group.<br /><br />Chemical formula for cuprite is <math> <msub>  <mtext>Cu</mtext>  <mtext>2</mtext> </msub> <mtext>O</mtext></math> and chemical formula of argentite is <math> <msub>  <mtext>Ag</mtext>  <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mtext>S</mtext></math>.<br /><br />Therefore, Argenite is not an oxide. Cuprite is an oxide mineral.<br /><br />Therefore, given statement is incorrect.",
